<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    One server choice in the redeem sheet.

    Inflated rather than constructed in code: Chip's three-argument
    constructor takes a defStyleAttr, not a style resource, so
    `Chip(context, null, R.style.Widget_PixelPayout_ServerChip)` silently
    drops the styling and renders a stock Material chip on a dark sheet.
    Inflating from a layout is the supported way to give a Chip a style.

    Deliberately has NO android:id. Every server chip comes from this one
    layout, so a fixed id would give them all the same one - and ChipGroup
    tracks its single selection by view id, so it could not then tell them
    apart. RedeemSheetFragment assigns a generated id to each.
-->
<com.google.android.material.chip.Chip xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    style="@style/Widget.PixelPayout.ServerChip"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:checkable="true"
    tools:text="Global" />
